<title>ITALY: Fiat outlines Alfa April temporary lay-offs.</title>
<headline>Fiat outlines Alfa April temporary lay-offs.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's carmaker Fiat Auto announced on Friday temporary worker layoff plans at its two Alfa Romeo car plants in Italy for a five-week period stretching from March 31 to May 4.</p>
<p>The temporary layoffs involve car workers at Alfa's plants at Arese, just north-west of Milan, and at Pomigliano D'Arco near Naples in the south of Italy.</p>
<p>A Fiat spokeswoman said that in the first two weeks the plan would include 3,500 workers, the third week 600 workers, while the fourth and fifth weeks it would involve some 2,500 workers. In total, it would mean some 5,000 less vehicles produced.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
